## Falcon reference implementation  (signer + keygen)

The `falcon` module's signing and key-generation cores are a faithful PORT of
the Falcon Round-3 reference implementation (Falcon-impl-20211101,
https://falcon-sign.info), done to reproduce the NIST Round-3 KAT vectors
byte-for-byte: `fpr.zig` (fpr.h/fpr.c constants + integer rounding), `fft.zig`
(fft.c), `gaussian.zig` (rng.c `prng_*`, sign.c `gaussian0`/`BerExp`/
`sampler`), `ffsampling.zig` (sign.c `ffSampling_fft_dyntree`/`do_sign_dyn`),
and `ntru.zig` (keygen.c: `mkgauss`, the `zint_*`/`modp_*` bignum-RNS layer,
and `solve_NTRU*`). The reference is under the MIT license, reproduced here as
its terms require:

